(5612870, 812988, 83313, '<td valign="top">Looks really odd. I see lots of artifacts, but the file size does not suggest excessive compression. Not sure if this is an intentional effect, or a reflection, or what...<br/> <br/>It''s possible that you repeatedly saved this as a JPEG during a number of editing sessions. If that is the case, the fix is to always save in an uncompressed format until you make your final save for upload. That would be either a TIF or your photo editors native format. PSD for Photoshop, PSPIMAGE for PaintShop Pro.</td>', 'Looks really odd. I see lots of artifacts, but the file size does not suggest excessive compression. Not sure if this is an intentional effect, or a reflection, or what... It''s possible that you repeatedly saved this as a JPEG during a number of editing sessions. If that is the case, the fix is to always save in an uncompressed format until you make your final save for upload. That would be either a TIF or your photo editors native format. PSD for Photoshop, PSPIMAGE for PaintShop Pro.', '2009-08-16 00:39:42.000000', NULL, 1),
