(5616265, 813259, 83313, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Alex_Europa:</b></div><hr/><i> I want to give a big thank you to those 37 of you that thought it really sucked, but didn''t let me know why. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>We have one of our resident programming nerds working on a javascript that will register an electric shock through the mouse for any vote of 3 or less without a comment.</td>', 'Originally posted by Alex_Europa: I want to give a big thank you to those 37 of you that thought it really sucked, but didn''t let me know why.  We have one of our resident programming nerds working on a javascript that will register an electric shock through the mouse for any vote of 3 or less without a comment.', '2009-08-19 02:35:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616274, 812903, 83313, '<td valign="top">Totally robbed, but you expected that, didn''t you? You achieved what you wanted with this shot. Just check out all the comments, especially that mine is the 5th one to come in shortly after the challenge. Very rare for something that places this close to the bottom. I would consider this entry a success.</td>', 'Totally robbed, but you expected that, didn''t you? You achieved what you wanted with this shot. Just check out all the comments, especially that mine is the 5th one to come in shortly after the challenge. Very rare for something that places this close to the bottom. I would consider this entry a success.', '2009-08-19 02:39:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616282, 813413, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''m sorry I failed to leave a comment for you during the challenge, however, you know I comment more on the low votes I leave. This got a 7 from me. I find it an excellent example of seeing the light. Sharp, clear, and smooth. The sub-5 score surprises me.</td>', 'I''m sorry I failed to leave a comment for you during the challenge, however, you know I comment more on the low votes I leave. This got a 7 from me. I find it an excellent example of seeing the light. Sharp, clear, and smooth. The sub-5 score surprises me.', '2009-08-19 02:43:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616291, 813422, 83313, '<td valign="top">In spite of the sub-5 score, I would call this a success. Just reading through the comments and looking at the commenter''s average tells me this worked well for a lot of people, and they appreciated the creativity.</td>', 'In spite of the sub-5 score, I would call this a success. Just reading through the comments and looking at the commenter''s average tells me this worked well for a lot of people, and they appreciated the creativity.', '2009-08-19 02:47:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616295, 812679, 83313, '<td valign="top">Placed way lower than I anticipated, but it may have lost some detail and clarity in the downsize to 640 pixels. At the size you originally showed it to me, I had figured it for a high 5 with no problem. (Of course, I have been known to be wrong before.)</td>', 'Placed way lower than I anticipated, but it may have lost some detail and clarity in the downsize to 640 pixels. At the size you originally showed it to me, I had figured it for a high 5 with no problem. (Of course, I have been known to be wrong before.)', '2009-08-19 02:50:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616307, 813324, 107410, '<td valign="top">I personally thought this was a great capture! Especially when one considers the band...well played, Sir. 9 and my vote for the posthumous!</td>', 'I personally thought this was a great capture! Especially when one considers the band...well played, Sir. 9 and my vote for the posthumous!', '2009-08-19 02:55:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616323, 813422, 107410, '<td valign="top">I would like to second Steve''s post-challenge comment. I think you did a great job with this shot and the sub-5 score is IMO, not at all reflective of the creativity and effort that you put into this capture. I definitely must applaud you for taking a really tough band name (and pulling if off)...instead of copping out with an easy one (like I did).<br/> <br/>ETA: Care to share how you did this?<br/> <br/>- Alex<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-08-19 02:06:24.</i></td>', 'I would like to second Steve''s post-challenge comment. I think you did a great job with this shot and the sub-5 score is IMO, not at all reflective of the creativity and effort that you put into this capture. I definitely must applaud you for taking a really tough band name (and pulling if off)...instead of copping out with an easy one (like I did). ETA: Care to share how you did this? - Alex', '2009-08-19 03:04:49.000000', '2009-08-19 03:06:24.000000', 0),
