(5616358, 812695, 17153, '<td valign="top">Yeah! Blur is getting recognized as a form of art! However, not just any blur, yours is simply fantastic!</td>', 'Yeah! Blur is getting recognized as a form of art! However, not just any blur, yours is simply fantastic!', '2009-08-19 03:23:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616362, 813301, 72134, '<td valign="top">Simple: "Sigur" means victory and "Ros" means rose.</td>', 'Simple: "Sigur" means victory and "Ros" means rose.', '2009-08-19 03:36:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616416, 813259, 54645, '<td valign="top">OK. I gave this a 4, basically because it met the challenge topic. 4 is my minimum vote for those that meet the topic. I do like the abstract feel, but as a whole I''m not drawn in to the photo. BW was a good choice. As far as processing, the halo around the nickel is too prominent, and it is legal to clone/heal sensor dust in basic.</td>', 'OK. I gave this a 4, basically because it met the challenge topic. 4 is my minimum vote for those that meet the topic. I do like the abstract feel, but as a whole I''m not drawn in to the photo. BW was a good choice. As far as processing, the halo around the nickel is too prominent, and it is legal to clone/heal sensor dust in basic.', '2009-08-19 04:17:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616520, 812974, 98186, '<td valign="top">You should try playing around with curves and levels in your editing program.  I would level the picture because it seems tilted.  Also, some contrast and a touch of saturation might help compensate for the washed out look.<br/> <br/>I love pictures of light shining through trees.  Very cool idea :)</td>', 'You should try playing around with curves and levels in your editing program.  I would level the picture because it seems tilted.  Also, some contrast and a touch of saturation might help compensate for the washed out look. I love pictures of light shining through trees.  Very cool idea :)', '2009-08-19 05:38:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616559, 813396, 98369, '<td valign="top">Never seen Hamilton looking so pretty.....great picture and Midnight oils is great</td>', 'Never seen Hamilton looking so pretty.....great picture and Midnight oils is great', '2009-08-19 06:18:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616569, 812679, 67152, '<td valign="top">A nice shot - a simple composition with a very pretty model - but the saturation is extreme, especially in the face where her skin almost appears orangish-pink and the details appear to be lacking a bit from the model and the wall.  I wonder if a slightly tighter crop on the right (to remove the small amount of sky) would have helped you out a bit on placing her more at the right third.</td>', 'A nice shot - a simple composition with a very pretty model - but the saturation is extreme, especially in the face where her skin almost appears orangish-pink and the details appear to be lacking a bit from the model and the wall.  I wonder if a slightly tighter crop on the right (to remove the small amount of sky) would have helped you out a bit on placing her more at the right third.', '2009-08-19 06:59:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616590, 813305, 37719, '<td valign="top">Excellent image!  Well done!</td>', 'Excellent image!  Well done!', '2009-08-19 07:17:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616647, 812903, 33909, '<td valign="top">I like this shot a lot, especially for the shock value it presents. About the score, well I guess that was to be expected... after all dpc''ers are usually way too easily offended...</td>', 'I like this shot a lot, especially for the shock value it presents. About the score, well I guess that was to be expected... after all dpc''ers are usually way too easily offended...', '2009-08-19 08:42:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616652, 813007, 81530, '<td valign="top">Lovely Shot. Congrats!</td>', 'Lovely Shot. Congrats!', '2009-08-19 08:51:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616654, 812996, 81530, '<td valign="top">Well done Oliver. I''ve always found your work to be inspiring. Keep it up.</td>', 'Well done Oliver. I''ve always found your work to be inspiring. Keep it up.', '2009-08-19 08:53:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616655, 813317, 81530, '<td valign="top">Lovely photo. You shared my top vote.</td>', 'Lovely photo. You shared my top vote.', '2009-08-19 08:53:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616656, 813305, 81530, '<td valign="top">Great shot Alain!</td>', 'Great shot Alain!', '2009-08-19 08:54:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616657, 812695, 81530, '<td valign="top">Lovely photograph. You shared my highest vote.</td>', 'Lovely photograph. You shared my highest vote.', '2009-08-19 08:54:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616661, 813214, 81530, '<td valign="top">One of my favourites from the challenge.</td>', 'One of my favourites from the challenge.', '2009-08-19 08:54:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616675, 813317, 8860, '<td valign="top">I wasn''t aware of the band  until recently after Googling it - but I liked the name. <br/> <br/>Vibrated the buoy cable to create ripples. <br/>Desaturated, boosted levels and cropped. As ever, done very quickly at the end of the last day when kids are asleep.<br/>---<br/> <br/>Thanks.<br/>: J<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-08-19 18:14:47.</i></td>', 'I wasn''t aware of the band  until recently after Googling it - but I liked the name.  Vibrated the buoy cable to create ripples. Desaturated, boosted levels and cropped. As ever, done very quickly at the end of the last day when kids are asleep.--- Thanks.: J', '2009-08-19 09:09:10.000000', '2009-08-19 19:14:47.000000', 0),
(5616677, 813396, 79720, '<td valign="top">Wow, what an awesome finish! Who knew Hamilton would be good for a ribbon? Certainly not anyone actually <i>living</i> there... <b>:</b>-P<br/> <br/>Major congrats, Jon....oskee-wee-wee!</td>', 'Wow, what an awesome finish! Who knew Hamilton would be good for a ribbon? Certainly not anyone actually living there... :-P Major congrats, Jon....oskee-wee-wee!', '2009-08-19 09:10:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616751, 813396, 96572, '<td valign="top">Hey! Congrats! Way to go!!!!!</td>', 'Hey! Congrats! Way to go!!!!!', '2009-08-19 10:08:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616758, 812768, 51269, '<td valign="top">Way to go , Anni !!!!  Excellent capture &amp; the bokeh is to die for !</td>', 'Way to go , Anni !!!!  Excellent capture & the bokeh is to die for !', '2009-08-19 10:14:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616766, 812679, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>Good name shot , well done<br/> <br/>The colours are over saturated making her tights a shocking pink which look almost luminous, the skin tones are fairly yellow/orangy.  The boots are to die for though!!<br/> <br/>you have an interesting background that really brings out your subject, a tighter crop would have helped with this shot, especially on the right hand side all the way to the window. <br/> <br/>Your details are good on teh wood, very nicely done</td>', 'Hi from the C Club Good name shot , well done The colours are over saturated making her tights a shocking pink which look almost luminous, the skin tones are fairly yellow/orangy.  The boots are to die for though!! you have an interesting background that really brings out your subject, a tighter crop would have helped with this shot, especially on the right hand side all the way to the window.  Your details are good on teh wood, very nicely done', '2009-08-19 10:24:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616771, 812514, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>Excellent shot, sharp clean details, very nicely sharpened.<br/> <br/>I think the only thing that is hurting this photo is the size.  Remember that you can go up to 640 on one side and the lower the resolution is the bigger your picture will be, so instead of 300, try 150 or even 100/  If you feel that you are losing details then go up.</td>', 'Hi from the C Club Excellent shot, sharp clean details, very nicely sharpened. I think the only thing that is hurting this photo is the size.  Remember that you can go up to 640 on one side and the lower the resolution is the bigger your picture will be, so instead of 300, try 150 or even 100/  If you feel that you are losing details then go up.', '2009-08-19 10:27:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616782, 813259, 87808, '<td valign="top">hi from teh shot club<br/> <br/>I am really surprised that this finished so low.  I liked this very much. <br/> <br/>Artistically, it is very clever.  Technically there are a couple of things that are wrong.  I think for this challenge having the face of the coin showing up a little more would have helped.  There is a lot of grain and some sensor dust going on. <br/> <br/>One tip for the blac and white is to saturate or use selective colours and play around with those before you change it to black and white, you will be surprised at what details come out this way. Unsharp mask would have also helped to bring out some details. <br/> <br/>the shallow DOF is a great choice for this. <br/> <br/>Yo-Spiff gave you an excellent comment below.<br/> <br/>I would love to see you redo this shot.</td>', 'hi from teh shot club I am really surprised that this finished so low.  I liked this very much.  Artistically, it is very clever.  Technically there are a couple of things that are wrong.  I think for this challenge having the face of the coin showing up a little more would have helped.  There is a lot of grain and some sensor dust going on.  One tip for the blac and white is to saturate or use selective colours and play around with those before you change it to black and white, you will be surprised at what details come out this way. Unsharp mask would have also helped to bring out some details.  the shallow DOF is a great choice for this.  Yo-Spiff gave you an excellent comment below. I would love to see you redo this shot.', '2009-08-19 10:35:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616790, 813007, 67343, '<td valign="top">Congrats this is beautiful.</td>', 'Congrats this is beautiful.', '2009-08-19 10:38:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616791, 812695, 70661, '<td valign="top">Awesome Juli! Congrats on catching this "happy accident"!</td>', 'Awesome Juli! Congrats on catching this "happy accident"!', '2009-08-19 10:38:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616818, 813007, 63244, '<td valign="top">Congrats! Gorgeous photograph! Well deserved!</td>', 'Congrats! Gorgeous photograph! Well deserved!', '2009-08-19 10:56:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616852, 813316, 79720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Yo_Spiff:</b></div><hr/><i> The greenish tone of the image does not come off well for me, I''m afraid. Looks like a thunderstorm is about to let loose. I wonder how this may have looked with a different treatment. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Wonder no longer, Spiffster...had it been more than basic, it might have been closer to this:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=815126" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/79720/120/815126.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/79720/120/815126.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/79720/120/815126.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Originally posted by Yo_Spiff: The greenish tone of the image does not come off well for me, I''m afraid. Looks like a thunderstorm is about to let loose. I wonder how this may have looked with a different treatment.  Wonder no longer, Spiffster...had it been more than basic, it might have been closer to this: ', '2009-08-19 11:20:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616860, 812514, 105555, '<td valign="top">Thank you JulietNN<br/> <br/>I still struggle to understand the basics of photo post-processing.  I didn''t know how to get a 150 k picture, neither that I could play with the quality.<br/> <br/>I will do that in the future...<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thank you JulietNN I still struggle to understand the basics of photo post-processing.  I didn''t know how to get a 150 k picture, neither that I could play with the quality. I will do that in the future... ', '2009-08-19 11:33:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5616985, 813227, 66384, '<td valign="top">That''s such an interesting story. I think the photo is excellent, and certainly does show the result of addiction. A trash can is a very symbolic place for an addict. This really makes a statement.<br/> <br/>I can''t really tell where she is from looking at the image, though. During voting, I thought she was coming out of a manhole. I don''t understand what is covering the top of her head either. That doesn''t diminish the impact of the image, but I think it did effect your score.<br/> <br/></td>', 'That''s such an interesting story. I think the photo is excellent, and certainly does show the result of addiction. A trash can is a very symbolic place for an addict. This really makes a statement. I can''t really tell where she is from looking at the image, though. During voting, I thought she was coming out of a manhole. I don''t understand what is covering the top of her head either. That doesn''t diminish the impact of the image, but I think it did effect your score. ', '2009-08-19 13:21:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617003, 813161, 66384, '<td valign="top">Black and white suits this image very well. I like the composition and contrast. It''s quite sad to think of a family losing three young sons. Can''t do it in basic editing, but now that the challenge is over, I''d recommend reducing the sharpening effect around the tree tops.</td>', 'Black and white suits this image very well. I like the composition and contrast. It''s quite sad to think of a family losing three young sons. Can''t do it in basic editing, but now that the challenge is over, I''d recommend reducing the sharpening effect around the tree tops.', '2009-08-19 13:29:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617007, 813296, 83026, '<td valign="top">I like this image. So eerie...</td>', 'I like this image. So eerie...', '2009-08-19 13:31:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617011, 813367, 66384, '<td valign="top">Love the colors here, and the textures. The sign does appear to be levitated. Perhaps that is the ''magic''. I think it was lost on most voters though. The image is great, I think the voters just didn''t connect it well with the challenge.</td>', 'Love the colors here, and the textures. The sign does appear to be levitated. Perhaps that is the ''magic''. I think it was lost on most voters though. The image is great, I think the voters just didn''t connect it well with the challenge.', '2009-08-19 13:33:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617035, 812679, 66384, '<td valign="top">I love the color of the wood. I think it would benefit from having the right side cropped a bit, removing the distracting light at the side of the building, and bringing the subject more off-center. Her outfit overpowers the blond hair, and I\''m suspecting that may have effected the score. I like the mystery of this shot: Why is she dressed like that in that location? Why is she leaning like that against the wall? What is on her mind?</td>', 'I love the color of the wood. I think it would benefit from having the right side cropped a bit, removing the distracting light at the side of the building, and bringing the subject more off-center. Her outfit overpowers the blond hair, and I\''m suspecting that may have effected the score. I like the mystery of this shot: Why is she dressed like that in that location? Why is she leaning like that against the wall? What is on her mind?', '2009-08-19 13:45:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617059, 812570, 66384, '<td valign="top">I like the simplicity of this and the diagonal tilt of the image. The title fits it very well. I think it would benefit vastly from a slight color adjustment. Using a color balance adjustment layer, slide the midtones and highlights from blue toward yellow. You''ll see an amazing but subtle change in the brightness of the image.</td>', 'I like the simplicity of this and the diagonal tilt of the image. The title fits it very well. I think it would benefit vastly from a slight color adjustment. Using a color balance adjustment layer, slide the midtones and highlights from blue toward yellow. You''ll see an amazing but subtle change in the brightness of the image.', '2009-08-19 13:57:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617069, 813194, 66384, '<td valign="top">Great ''Norman Rockwell'' image. Love the processing, and the b&amp;w suits it well. It really makes me smile!</td>', 'Great ''Norman Rockwell'' image. Love the processing, and the b&w suits it well. It really makes me smile!', '2009-08-19 14:01:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617135, 813007, 91783, '<td valign="top">i love this band. and congrats. beautiful photo. who could give this shot a 1? seems silly. congrats again!</td>', 'i love this band. and congrats. beautiful photo. who could give this shot a 1? seems silly. congrats again!', '2009-08-19 14:38:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617146, 813316, 91783, '<td valign="top">i like this image a lot. not only because of the band...but because of the composition, the tones. just love the image.<br/></td>', 'i like this image a lot. not only because of the band...but because of the composition, the tones. just love the image.', '2009-08-19 14:41:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617154, 813007, 59276, '<td valign="top">love to see this on the front page........wonderful tight crop.</td>', 'love to see this on the front page........wonderful tight crop.', '2009-08-19 14:45:55.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5617162, 813007, 8891, '<td valign="top">Exquisite! Big congrats on your new blue!</td>', 'Exquisite! Big congrats on your new blue!', '2009-08-19 14:49:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617200, 813422, 49954, '<td valign="top">This is a four second exposure -- lit by the modelling light on my Alien Bees light.<br/> <br/>After the shutter opened, I started moving the word EYE (cut from cardstock) then I counted to about 3.5 and held position, then triggered the flash with the remote handheld.<br/> <br/>Converted to B&amp;W with gradient map, then adjusted the opacity of the layer to make it more a dreamy feel.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the kind comments and those who appreciated the effort!</td>', 'This is a four second exposure -- lit by the modelling light on my Alien Bees light. After the shutter opened, I started moving the word EYE (cut from cardstock) then I counted to about 3.5 and held position, then triggered the flash with the remote handheld. Converted to B&W with gradient map, then adjusted the opacity of the layer to make it more a dreamy feel. Thanks for the kind comments and those who appreciated the effort!', '2009-08-19 15:06:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617224, 812695, 50695, '<td valign="top">damn... that''s phenomenal. sorry I didn''t vote.</td>', 'damn... that''s phenomenal. sorry I didn''t vote.', '2009-08-19 15:33:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617233, 812695, 23098, '<td valign="top">Didn''t vote on this challenge but if I had this would''ve caught my attention.  Beautiful shot.  Congrats on the top 10 finish.</td>', 'Didn''t vote on this challenge but if I had this would''ve caught my attention.  Beautiful shot.  Congrats on the top 10 finish.', '2009-08-19 15:39:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617289, 812996, 9114, '<td valign="top">I love seeing setup shots.<br/>Great image and thanks for sharing<br/>Debbi</td>', 'I love seeing setup shots.Great image and thanks for sharingDebbi', '2009-08-19 16:19:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617319, 813324, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club, <br/> <br/>I like your abstract, mainly because I can still tell what it is. Excellent work. <br/> <br/>There is nothing that I can think of that you can do with the shot technically wise, but in post processing maybe playing with the selective colours could have made this a little more vibrant. It may have helped with the blown out highlights you have on the bottom left. I am not a huge fan of borders, but I think this one could take it. <br/> <br/>Nice job!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the C Club,  I like your abstract, mainly because I can still tell what it is. Excellent work.  There is nothing that I can think of that you can do with the shot technically wise, but in post processing maybe playing with the selective colours could have made this a little more vibrant. It may have helped with the blown out highlights you have on the bottom left. I am not a huge fan of borders, but I think this one could take it.  Nice job! ', '2009-08-19 16:47:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617327, 813305, 24454, '<td valign="top">This is really good!  I love all that magical red.</td>', 'This is really good!  I love all that magical red.', '2009-08-19 16:54:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617333, 812695, 24454, '<td valign="top">Oh Juli!  THIS is fine art at its best.  I hope this means our fellow dpc''ers are coming around about the artistry of well done blur!  You certainly show how its done here!  Congratulations on 7th place (even tho I would have given it a ribbon if it were up to me) !<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oh Juli!  THIS is fine art at its best.  I hope this means our fellow dpc''ers are coming around about the artistry of well done blur!  You certainly show how its done here!  Congratulations on 7th place (even tho I would have given it a ribbon if it were up to me) ! ', '2009-08-19 16:56:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617350, 812903, 87808, '<td valign="top">C Club here, <br/> <br/>Not a lot I can say really about this photograph.  It is in focus, dof is good, saturation is good, lighting is good. You got what you wanted with this shot by shocking people.  <br/> <br/></td>', 'C Club here,  Not a lot I can say really about this photograph.  It is in focus, dof is good, saturation is good, lighting is good. You got what you wanted with this shot by shocking people.   ', '2009-08-19 17:10:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617387, 813422, 99506, '<td valign="top">You were robbed, this was a great entry</td>', 'You were robbed, this was a great entry', '2009-08-19 18:01:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617393, 813007, 76712, '<td valign="top">i knew you would win i voted 10 well done!</td>', 'i knew you would win i voted 10 well done!', '2009-08-19 18:06:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617404, 812209, 67258, '<td valign="top">Ha! Stiff Little Fingers were the very first band I saw, in 1978, supporting the Tom Robinson Band, just before Inflammable Material came out.  Saw them again in 1979.  Excellent stuff!</td>', 'Ha! Stiff Little Fingers were the very first band I saw, in 1978, supporting the Tom Robinson Band, just before Inflammable Material came out.  Saw them again in 1979.  Excellent stuff!', '2009-08-19 18:12:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617436, 813422, 49954, '<td valign="top">Thanks Lutchenko... comments from you and some other high scorers here are prized above ribbons. :)<br/> <br/>I think some thought it was illegal, others recognized me :), others didn''t know what R.E.M. meant... who knows.  When the scores were first getting announced, I figured above 5 would do very well... came close to five, but closer to the bottom <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-08-19 17:34:42.</i></td>', 'Thanks Lutchenko... comments from you and some other high scorers here are prized above ribbons. :) I think some thought it was illegal, others recognized me :), others didn''t know what R.E.M. meant... who knows.  When the scores were first getting announced, I figured above 5 would do very well... came close to five, but closer to the bottom ', '2009-08-19 18:33:33.000000', '2009-08-19 18:34:42.000000', 0),
(5617457, 813389, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club, <br/> <br/>Fun shot fits your title and challenge. <br/> <br/>Your lighting is a little harsh in this shot, I would bouncing a light or a different angle.  Even in post processing you can adjust the exposure, which in this case may have been the way to go.<br/> <br/>A tighter crop off the top would have helped with the DOF and POV here. Cropping off the bottom would get rid of the line that separates the shot.  You kinda chopped yoru knuckles off too!!<br/> <br/>I would suggest a play with exposure, brightness and contrast and shadows and highlights to make this photo pop a little more, it is fairly flat right now. <br/> <br/>Great capture of the flames.</td>', 'Hi from the C Club,  Fun shot fits your title and challenge.  Your lighting is a little harsh in this shot, I would bouncing a light or a different angle.  Even in post processing you can adjust the exposure, which in this case may have been the way to go. A tighter crop off the top would have helped with the DOF and POV here. Cropping off the bottom would get rid of the line that separates the shot.  You kinda chopped yoru knuckles off too!! I would suggest a play with exposure, brightness and contrast and shadows and highlights to make this photo pop a little more, it is fairly flat right now.  Great capture of the flames.', '2009-08-19 18:58:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617578, 813007, 20331, '<td valign="top">I really admire this photo! Could you upload it to DPC prints so I can order a copy for my home? Excellent!</td>', 'I really admire this photo! Could you upload it to DPC prints so I can order a copy for my home? Excellent!', '2009-08-19 21:36:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617710, 812996, 79955, '<td valign="top">Congrats Oliver , brilliant setup , brilliant shot!</td>', 'Congrats Oliver , brilliant setup , brilliant shot!', '2009-08-19 23:16:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617787, 812490, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Meeting the challenge in this particular contest is sort of a given, so in order to do well, there are a couple other requirements.  I can see the relationship between your band name and your photo, but beyond that, the image doesn''t provide any significant impact to the viewer (me).  Your focus on the subject is good, but compositionally, the image simply lacks interest.  The cage corner in the lower left portion of the frame blocks the subject and creates, for lack of a more refined term, a distraction within the frame.  It''s unfortunate that you didn''t receive any feedback on this image in the challenge that is worth reading, but that seems to happen frequently on images that are not ''bad'' but not ''good'' either.  Middle of the road images don''t garner much in the form of comments from the walmart shoppers.  <br/> <br/>As with any photograph, high levels of visual and/or emotional impact are the foundations for building a strong photo.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... Meeting the challenge in this particular contest is sort of a given, so in order to do well, there are a couple other requirements.  I can see the relationship between your band name and your photo, but beyond that, the image doesn''t provide any significant impact to the viewer (me).  Your focus on the subject is good, but compositionally, the image simply lacks interest.  The cage corner in the lower left portion of the frame blocks the subject and creates, for lack of a more refined term, a distraction within the frame.  It''s unfortunate that you didn''t receive any feedback on this image in the challenge that is worth reading, but that seems to happen frequently on images that are not ''bad'' but not ''good'' either.  Middle of the road images don''t garner much in the form of comments from the walmart shoppers.   As with any photograph, high levels of visual and/or emotional impact are the foundations for building a strong photo.', '2009-08-20 00:27:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617889, 812514, 76430, '<td valign="top">If you use Photoshop check out the tutorial on <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">preparing a photograph for DPChallenge</a>.  If you use something else you can probably get some hints from it that will help you.</td>', 'If you use Photoshop check out the tutorial on preparing a photograph for DPChallenge.  If you use something else you can probably get some hints from it that will help you.', '2009-08-20 02:31:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5618052, 812994, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C CLub<br/> <br/>Nice looking bird there!<br/> <br/>There is something about this shot that just feels a little off.  I think it is the straight lines behind it. They are throwing the bird off and making it look like it should be straightened out. I think a squarer crop may have helped this a little with that issue.  The bird looks great, sharp and clean.  I would like to have seen you zoom in a little bit more on this as you have such good clarity on the head. In post processing, the selective colours, colour balance and curves would have pushed those colours on the wing nicely. Maybe, just maybe exposue and contrast with a touch of gamma would have deleted your background somewhat. <br/> <br/>Nice shot, well done</td>', 'Hi from the C CLub Nice looking bird there! There is something about this shot that just feels a little off.  I think it is the straight lines behind it. They are throwing the bird off and making it look like it should be straightened out. I think a squarer crop may have helped this a little with that issue.  The bird looks great, sharp and clean.  I would like to have seen you zoom in a little bit more on this as you have such good clarity on the head. In post processing, the selective colours, colour balance and curves would have pushed those colours on the wing nicely. Maybe, just maybe exposue and contrast with a touch of gamma would have deleted your background somewhat.  Nice shot, well done', '2009-08-20 09:06:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5618485, 813161, 16912, '<td valign="top">Greetings from Andi via the Critique Club<br/> <br/><b>First Impression:</b> Hmm, have looked at this for a while now and the jury is still out on whether I like it or not.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> I like the composition and the foreground stone leaning helps give impact to the image. I''m wondering if an even lower perspective would help chop the trees from the top of the foreground stone?<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> I did wonder if this had been an idea for the death challenge and it might even have score better in it. I''ve never heard of the band (am an old man now) but am sure its out there ;)<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b>I think this is the area that confused me when first viewing the image. The ''issue'' here is the image appears to have been oversharpened - probably to allow us to read more of the gravestone however, it messed with the treetops, the edge of the gravestone and also the grass bottom right. I like the lighting on the foreground gravestone but it looks false on the background stone.<br/> <br/><b>Final thoughts:</b> I didn''t vote in this challenge but would probably have left a 5. Now, if you had taken the image on a moonlit night with some moody clouds then a 6 would have been my starting point. BTW, you should try a lensbaby, they are made for images like this!</td>', 'Greetings from Andi via the Critique Club First Impression: Hmm, have looked at this for a while now and the jury is still out on whether I like it or not. Composition: I like the composition and the foreground stone leaning helps give impact to the image. I''m wondering if an even lower perspective would help chop the trees from the top of the foreground stone? Subject: I did wonder if this had been an idea for the death challenge and it might even have score better in it. I''ve never heard of the band (am an old man now) but am sure its out there ;) Technical:I think this is the area that confused me when first viewing the image. The ''issue'' here is the image appears to have been oversharpened - probably to allow us to read more of the gravestone however, it messed with the treetops, the edge of the gravestone and also the grass bottom right. I like the lighting on the foreground gravestone but it looks false on the background stone. Final thoughts: I didn''t vote in this challenge but would probably have left a 5. Now, if you had taken the image on a moonlit night with some moody clouds then a 6 would have been my starting point. BTW, you should try a lensbaby, they are made for images like this!', '2009-08-20 17:36:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5618699, 812996, 49643, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! Very well executed shot!</td>', 'Congratulations! Very well executed shot!', '2009-08-20 22:44:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5618701, 813007, 49643, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! Beautiful exposure &amp; details!</td>', 'Congratulations! Beautiful exposure & details!', '2009-08-20 22:46:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5618999, 812996, 79838, '<td valign="top">very nice shot !!<br/>congratulations on your ribbon, very well deserved.</td>', 'very nice shot !!congratulations on your ribbon, very well deserved.', '2009-08-21 09:04:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5619255, 813134, 55005, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First impression -- love the image, the tones and the light. Agree with the commenters about the sheet, I think it costed you quite a few points, unfortunately. <br/> <br/>Techinicals -- I really love the light here. I would have like to see it as a more central composition, with rose and the gun equal distance from the edge. The focus is spot on, while the exposure on the model is good, the background seems a bit underexposed to me and is too similar in tone with the skin of the model.   <br/> <br/>Final thoughts -- I love the muted colors and the feel of the photo. Great composition and light. Good work.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions.<br/> <br/>Cheers, <br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First impression -- love the image, the tones and the light. Agree with the commenters about the sheet, I think it costed you quite a few points, unfortunately.  Techinicals -- I really love the light here. I would have like to see it as a more central composition, with rose and the gun equal distance from the edge. The focus is spot on, while the exposure on the model is good, the background seems a bit underexposed to me and is too similar in tone with the skin of the model.    Final thoughts -- I love the muted colors and the feel of the photo. Great composition and light. Good work. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions. Cheers,  Anna', '2009-08-21 13:13:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5619368, 813396, 35357, '<td valign="top">Congrats.  I shot a zoom-in! :-P<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=743399" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/945/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_743399.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/945/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_743399.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/945/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_743399.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Congrats.  I shot a zoom-in! :-P ', '2009-08-21 14:38:23.000000', NULL, 0),
